st decide what run_id is without guidance"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"State that runner.py reads the trace_id from req.config.trace_id (the RunRequest's LLMConfig, built from the resolved gate cfg) at both :259 and :719, noting FakeRunner has no self._config and already reaches config only via req.config.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.4,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["runner.py:246-265 — FakeRunner.run: __init__ (231-241) takes only findings/summary/structured, no LLMConfig; the only config in scope is req.config (used at line 264 as req.config.repo_path).","runner.py:366,379 — PydanticAIRunner.run derives cfg = _effective_config(self._config, req); self._config is the config passed at construction, NOT a resolve_gate_config() read.","runner.py:84 — RunRequest.config: LLMConfig; ops build RunRequest(config=<resolved cfg>) (operations.py:209-212), so req.config.trace_id is the value available at both sites.","ABSENCE: the plan asserts the contextvar reaches gate ops via resolve_gate_config, but never states how the value crosses into the runner — leaving self._config (undefined on FakeRunner) vs req.config vs a new resolve_gate_config() call inside the runner ambiguous."],"finding":"The plan directs threading the resolved trace_id into runner.py:259 and :719 but does not name the seam by which the runner obtains it; the runner never calls resolve_gate_config, and line 259 is inside FakeRunner.run which holds no LLMConfig.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f0f0de51c1427477b","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach section: 'Populate the verdict by threading the resolved identity's trace_id into the existing trace_id= arguments at src/rebar/llm/runner.py:259 and :719'","norm_id":"n48e6a047158c1cd0","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An implementer reads trace_id from self._config, which is unset on FakeRunner (AttributeError or missing field) and the structured/fake verdict path at :254 still emits null.","An implementer adds a resolve_gate_config() call inside runner.py, a new data path the plan's propagation argument does not cover and which behaves differently for standalone ops."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Amend the Approach to read `trace_id=req.config.trace_id` at both runner.py sites, since the resolved gate config flows into the op's RunRequest.config (operations.py:209-212) and FakeRunner.run already sources config from req.config (repo_path at :264) rather than an instance config.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"high"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add the two schema files to Scope and update the `trace_id` description in review_result.schema.json:31 and completion_verdict.schema.json:78 to describe the rebar-minted per-run correlation id (W3C 32-hex shape, present inside any gate run) instead of a Langfuse-only trace id.","cohort":["T8"],"criteria":["T8"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.3,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["review_result.schema.json:31: `\"trace_id\": { \"type\": [\"string\",\"null\"], \"description\": \"Langfuse trace id, when tracing is enabled; null otherwise.\" }`","completion_verdict.schema.json:78: identical 'Langfuse trace id when tracing is enabled; null otherwise' description","Plan Approach: identity 'carries trace_id (32 hex characters, lowercase, from secrets.token_hex(16))' and is minted per gate run — not a Langfuse trace id and not gated on tracing-enabled","Plan Scope lists config.py, gate_dispatch.py, runner.py, and the new test but NOT the two schema files, so the descriptions are never revised"],"finding":"The plan changes the emitted meaning of `trace_id` (from a Langfuse trace id populated only when tracing is enabled, to a rebar-minted per-run correlation id populated whenever inside a gate run) but does not update the schema field descriptions that define that vocabulary, leaving the contract's documented semantics contradicting the emitted value.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f0e561f50b1f44d6f","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / Scope; src/rebar/schemas/review_result.schema.json:31 and src/rebar/schemas/completion_verdict.schema.json:78","norm_id":"n50beaf60f809339f","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A downstream consumer or model reading the schema description treats trace_id as a Langfuse identifier and tries to resolve it in Langfuse, but it is a random rebar correlation id with no Langfuse trace behind it.","A reader sees a non-null trace_id and infers tracing was enabled, which the new semantics no longer imply."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Revise both `trace_id` descriptions to: 'Per-gate-run correlation id (32 lowercase hex, W3C trace-id shape) minted at the run boundary; null for standalone (non-gate-run) ops.' and add both schema files to the Scope list.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Either add covering criteria (and a named consumer) for ticket_id/operation/run_id, or drop them from the identity if only trace_id is consumed.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5e"],"criteria":["E1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":0.05,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["All six ACs concern only trace_id (equality, inequality, 32-hex shape, pool propagation, verdict field, None-outside-run)","No AC or described consumer references ticket_id, operation, or run_id on the identity"],"finding":"The identity carries ticket_id, operation, and run_id as described deliverables, but no acceptance criterion verifies any of these three fields (only trace_id is asserted), and the plan names no consumer for them.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f55a7dec0e0656969","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria vs Approach ('The identity carries trace_id, ticket_id, operation, and run_id')","norm_id":"n2c8dad27813b258c","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An implementer populates ticket_id/operation/run_id with no test guarding them and no downstream reader"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add an acceptance criterion that a completion-verifier verdict (runner.py:719) carries the run's trace_id and validates against completion_verdict.schema.json, not only the plan-review path against review_result.schema.json.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T5b","T6","T9","necessity","project.portability"],"criteria":["E5"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":0.05,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'thread the resolved identity's trace_id into the existing trace_id= arguments at src/rebar/llm/runner.py:259 and :719'","Plan cites both completion_verdict.schema.json and review_result.schema.json in Context, but the AC validator only runs review_result.schema.json","Both :259 and :719 are changed sites, so the completion-verifier verdict is changed behavior lacking a corresponding validation test"],"finding":"The plan changes verdict trace_id population at BOTH runner.py:259 (plan-review, review_result.schema.json) and :719 (completion-verifier, completion_verdict.schema.json), but the schema-validation acceptance criterion names only review_result.schema.json — the completion-verifier verdict path has no test asserting it carries trace_id and validates against completion_verdict.schema.json.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fc47893a51bb3235c","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria — 'A produced gate verdict carries the run's trace_id ... validates against review_result.schema.json'","norm_id":"n2ebfd52d99fdd6b2","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["completion-verifier gate run: verdict populated with trace_id but never validated against completion_verdict.schema.json, so a shape/format mismatch on that path closes green"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Extend the verdict-population AC to cover both run boundaries: one test for the plan-review verdict against review_result.schema.json and one for the completion-verifier verdict against completion_verdict.schema.json.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Justify each of `ticket_id`, `operation`, and `run_id` against a current consumer/AC, or drop them and mint only the `trace_id` the done-definition actually uses.","cohort":["A1"],"criteria":["A1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":0.05,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["The Scope, Testing, and all six Acceptance Criteria reference only `trace_id` (e.g. 'A produced gate verdict carries the run's `trace_id`'); `ticket_id`/`operation`/`run_id` appear nowhere as a consumer, verdict field, or test assertion.","Verdict population at runner.py:719 threads only `trace_id=`; there is no verdict field named for the other three.","YAGNI: fields that serve no current done-definition are premature — they add per-field state to LLMConfig for a hypothetical future reader."],"finding":"The minted identity carries `ticket_id`, `operation`, and `run_id` alongside `trace_id`, but none of these three is consumed anywhere in the plan's done-definition — only `trace_id` is threaded to the verdict and asserted in the ACs.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fcd5945c5b507b0de","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — 'The identity carries `trace_id` ... `ticket_id`, `operation`, and `run_id`.'","norm_id":"n96ff2579206771d0","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Reviewer/maintainer adds and carries three fields no code path reads, then must guess their intended semantics later."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Scope the identity to the single `trace_id` the verdict and ACs consume; defer `ticket_id`/`operation`/`run_id` to the ticket that first reads them.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add `runner.py:254` (FakeRunner structured-mode `\"trace_id\": None`) to the patch-site inventory, or state why the fake-runner verdict path is exempt from carrying the run trace_id.","cohort":["project.symbol-reference-completeness"],"criteria":["project.symbol-reference-completeness"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":0.1,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'replacing the hardcoded None' at 'src/rebar/llm/runner.py:259 and :719'","runner.py:254: `return {**payload, \"runner\": self.name, \"model\": None, \"trace_id\": None, \"_usage\": {}}` — a third verdict-producing trace_id=None site in FakeRunner.run() structured mode, not named in the plan","runner.py:226-227 documents FakeRunner as the seam that lets ops be 'tested end-to-end without the agents extra or an API key'"],"finding":"The plan enumerates the verdict `trace_id=None` patch sites as exactly `runner.py:259` and `:719`, but omits `runner.py:254` — the FakeRunner structured-mode return `{**payload, \"runner\": self.name, \"model\": None, \"trace_id\": None, \"_usage\": {}}`. FakeRunner is the DI seam used to run ops end-to-end without an API key (runner.py:226-227), and completion verification runs in `mode=\"structured\"`, so an in-process verdict is produced through line 254.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"feb23315466e9b5cc","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / Scope: 'Populate the verdict by threading the resolved identity's trace_id into the existing trace_id= arguments at src/rebar/llm/runner.py:259 and :719'","norm_id":"ndc813a9e5b03c220","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The plan's AC test 'A produced gate verdict carries the run's trace_id' — run in-process without an API key via the FakeRunner structured path (line 254) — would receive trace_id null and fail, or (if patched only at 259/719) the fake path silently keeps emitting null for every structured-mode verdict."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Thread the resolved identity's trace_id into the FakeRunner structured return at runner.py:254 as well as :259 and :719, so verdicts produced through the DI seam (which the plan's in-process AC tests exercise) carry the run trace_id.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Reconcile the new `run_id` with the existing workflow `new_run_id()`/`StepContext.run_id` — reuse it, or state explicitly why a separate per-run id on LLMConfig is required.","cohort":["A1"],"criteria":["A1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.4475,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["executor.py:82 `new_run_id()` returns `{ns-timestamp}-{uuid4hex}`, 'Generated ONCE per run and persisted on every WORKFLOW_RUN/STEP event'.","The existing run_id is threaded as `StepContext.run_id` (interpreter.py:217/394, executor.py:126/238) and used as the idempotency token (steps.py:262 `[rebar-run {run_id}/{step_id}]`, runs.py:461).","The plan neither cites this existing run_id nor explains why a second, differently-shaped one is needed on LLMConfig."],"finding":"The plan introduces a new per-run `run_id` field while rebar already mints a per-run run identity (`new_run_id()`), threaded as `StepContext.run_id` and used as the persisted idempotency key a